      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "What is the volume of a rectangular solid that has length, width, and height of $\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{ft},$ $\\sqrt{10}\\,\\text{ft},$ and $2\\,\\text{ft},$ respectively?",
      "worked_solution": "We can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV=lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nl=\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{ft},\\,w=\\sqrt{10}\\,\\text{ft},\\,h=2\\,\\text{ft}\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\nV=\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{10}\\cdot 2=2\\sqrt{50}=10\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{ft}}^{3}.\n$$",
